o engineering have been lacking. We selected a nanobody that potentially targets the conformational changes of the Hedgehog receptor Patched1 and demonstrated that this nanobody potently activates the pathway in vivo. This nanobody can serve as the basis for mechanistic studies of Hedgehog pathway activation and for potential therapeutic applications. Our method may further apply to the investigation of other related transporters in the Resistance-Nodulation-Division superfamily.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1073\/pnas.2011560117","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2020,11,2]],"date-time":"2020-11-02T20:32:23Z","timestamp":1604349143000},"page":"28838-28846","update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1073\/pnas.cm10313","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":37,"title":["Hedgehog pathway activation through nanobody-mediated conformational blockade of the Patched sterol conduit"],"prefix":"10.1073","volume":"117","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-2145-4151","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Yunxiao","family":"Zhang","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Institute for Stem Cell Biology and Regenerative Medicine, Stanford University School of Medicine, Stanford, CA 94305;"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-2186-9800","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Wan-Jin","family":"Lu","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Institute for Stem Cell Biology and Regenerative Medicine, Stanford University School of Medicine, Stanford, CA 94305;"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"David P.","family":"Bulkley","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Biochemistry and Biophysics, University of California, San Francisco, CA 94158;"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Jiahao","family":"Liang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Pharmaceutical Chemistry, University of California, San